	(text_box "With the VCU128 and TPX4 in data driven mode the supported channels are\n  Top serial out: any combination of (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7)  (4 & 7 may less clean)\n  Bot serial out: any combination of (0, 1, 4, 6)\n\nWith the VCU128 and TPX4 in frame based mode the supported channels are\n  Top serial out: any 1, 2, or 4 channels from (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7)  (4 & 7 may be less clean)\n  Bot serial out: any 1, 2, or 4 channels from (0, 1, 4, 6)\n\n\nMix AC coupling can be replaced by 0 ohm shorts in case DC works better with the receiving FPGA (VCU128' or SPIDR4 FPGA board).\n\nAC coupling caps for Bottom Channel 3 are DNP for VCU128 use.  If this board drives the SPIDR IV FPGA board install the AC coupling caps or 0 ohm jumpers.\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 508 147.32 0)
		(size -149.86 78.74)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
